"verified"}],"notes":"Native source occurrence; actual static and visual checks separate."},{"element_id":"E00057","element_type":"footnote","metadata_pointer":"/footnotes/0/exact_text","occurrences":[{"occurrence_id":"E00057O","docx_locator":"bookmark:E00057","source_text":"N ote: [1] For chemotherapy drugs, Relative dose intensity (%) = (Actual dose intensity / Planned dose intensity)*100, Actual dose intensity (mg/m^2/frequency) = Actual cumulative\ndose / Body surface area (BSA) / Total frequency of drug administration, According to the high ratio formula, Body surface area (BSA) =0.007184 × Weight (kg)0.425× Height(cm)0.725.\nThe last valid weight value and height value measured before each chemotherapy cycle will be used for calculating Body surface area (BSA).","role":"footnote","panel_id":"P122","source_ref_ids":["EV00057"],"verification_status":"verified"}],"notes":"Native source occurrence; actual static and visual checks separate."},{"element_id":"E00058","element_type":"programming_note","metadata_pointer":null,"occurrences":[{"occurrence_id":"E00058O","docx_locator":"bookmark:E00058","source_text":"Programming notes: relative dose intensity (%) is rounded to integer, and statistics for decimal places refer to SAP.","role":"programming_note","panel_id":"P122","source_ref_ids":["EV00058"],"verification_status":"verified"}],"notes":"Native source occurrence; actual static and visual checks separate."}],"occurrence_relations":[],"issues":[]}
